{
	title: 'rm -rf of scratch paths runs without approval',
	spec: 'Setting scratch (text, default /tmp/**) holds space-separated glob patterns (Bun.Glob, ~/ allowed) of paths rm -rf may delete without approval; /tmp/* still asks. Targets expand as the shell does: ~/, and $VAR set earlier in the command to a literal absolute or ~/ path; a cd to such a path makes relative targets known as before. Targets with .. (may cross a symlink) or unknown variables still ask. Rationale: 34 of 44 rm -rf prompts in Oct 24 - Nov 12 histories were for disposable scratch dirs; host-specific patterns live in the gitignored config.ason.',
